    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Nestled on the charming and historic Rock Street in the heart of Cloyne, College House is an impressive period residence that effortlessly blends character, space and modern convenience. This beautifully presented terraced home extends to generous proportions and offers flexible accommodation ideally suited to growing families, multi-generational living or those seeking space to work from home.\r\n\r\nBehind its attractive façade, the property has been painstakingly renovated to an exceptionally high standard over the years and is beautifully maintained and tastefully decorated throughout. Rich in original character, the home boasts high ceilings, beautiful timber panelling and a host of period features that create a warm and elegant atmosphere throughout.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises five spacious bedrooms, two bathrooms, two comfortable reception rooms and a bright, welcoming kitchen. The bathrooms are finished with high-quality sanitary ware, reflecting the care and attention to detail evident throughout the property.\r\n\r\nThe living accommodation is both warm and inviting, with two solid fuel stoves providing cosy focal points within the home. The living room is particularly impressive, featuring an original ornate slate fireplace with a cast-iron stove, adding charm and character to this elegant space. A second stove is located in the kitchen, creating a welcoming heart to the home. The property benefits from an electric heating system, while an air conditioning unit in the kitchen provides additional comfort throughout the year.\r\n\r\nOne of the standout features of College House is its exceptional outdoor space. To the side of the property, a private gated entrance provides secure off-street parking together with an EV charging point, a highly desirable feature for modern living. To the rear lies a generous sun-drenched garden, offering an ideal setting for outdoor dining, gardening, entertaining or simply relaxing in a private and peaceful environment.\r\n\r\nSituated in the picturesque village of Cloyne, the property enjoys all the benefits of village living while remaining within easy reach of larger urban centres. Cloyne is renowned for its rich history, strong community spirit and excellent local amenities, including shops, cafés, schools, sporting facilities and everyday services. The village is perhaps best known for the iconic Cloyne Round Tower, one of the finest examples of its kind in Ireland.\r\n\r\nThe thriving market town of Midleton is approximately 15 minutes away by car and offers a superb range of amenities including major supermarkets, restaurants, boutiques, schools and rail connections to Cork City. Cork City itself is within approximately 35–40 minutes' drive, making College House an attractive option for commuters seeking a balance between town and country living. The renowned Ballymaloe area is within easy reach, while the beautiful East Cork coastline, with its beaches, harbours, scenic walks and coastal villages, is also readily accessible.\r\n\r\nCombining generous accommodation, period character, modern conveniences and an enviable village location, College House presents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a distinctive family home in one of East Cork's most sought-after locations.\r\n\r\nFeatures\r\n\r\nElegant period residence\r\nFive spacious bedrooms\r\nTwo bathrooms with high-quality sanitary ware throughout\r\nTwo reception rooms\r\nOriginal ornate slate fireplace with cast-iron stove in living room\r\nBeautiful timber panelling\r\nHigh ceilings throughout\r\nPainstakingly renovated to an exceptionally high standard\r\nPrivate side access with secure gated off-street parking\r\nEV charging point\r\nLarge sun-drenched rear garden\r\nTwo solid fuel stoves\r\nElectric heating system\r\nAir conditioning unit in kitchen\r\nBeautifully presented and tastefully decorated throughout\r\nWalking distance to village amenities\r\nClose to Ballymaloe and the East Cork coastline\r\nApproximately 15 minutes from Midleton\r\nApproximately 35–40 minutes from Cork City\r\n\r\nBER C1\r\nBER Number: 111583258\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the character, scale and superb location of this unique home."
      },
